1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,465
This is the Ngao Exploration Console

2
00:00:03,465 --> 00:00:10,390
a mineral targeting workbench for Tanzania, developed under AD Ports Group's research and innovation programme.

3
00:00:10,590 --> 00:00:15,383
Choose a commodity, and hyperspectral satellite imagery builds a heat map of concentration

4
00:00:15,383 --> 00:00:19,420
reading minerals directly, and through their signature in vegetation.

5
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:22,395
Every ministry licence is overlaid on that surface

6
00:00:22,395 --> 00:00:24,129
each with a passport:

7
00:00:24,129 --> 00:00:27,600
holder, declared minerals, and what has actually been excavated.

8
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:30,424
Roads, railways, ports and power complete the picture;

9
00:00:30,424 --> 00:00:34,710
a single AI score then ranks every block on the same basis.

10
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:36,924
The result is open ground, ranked:

11
00:00:36,924 --> 00:00:39,285
high anomaly, best access, not yet taken

12
00:00:39,285 --> 00:00:42,670
with a peg application drafted in one click.

13
00:00:42,870 --> 00:00:45,589
Our own licences track the field crews

14
00:00:45,589 --> 00:00:47,143
drilling, gravity, geophysics

15
00:00:47,143 --> 00:00:50,600
with every geological report one click away.

16
00:00:50,810 --> 00:00:53,163
And the laboratory queue shows the backlog

17
00:00:53,163 --> 00:00:55,179
thousands of samples past promise

18
00:00:55,179 --> 00:00:57,210
so nothing stalls unseen.

19
00:00:57,410 --> 00:01:00,670
Ngao. Find the licence before anyone else does.

